  "responseTimeMs": 11244,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nTo claim a bad debt as a deductible expense, a corporation must demonstrate that the debt is considered worthless and that it has been previously included in gross income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, corporations must maintain adequate documentation to support their claims of bad debts, including evidence of the debt's worthlessness and proof of its prior inclusion in gross income. This may involve providing records of collection efforts and any relevant communications with the debtor. Proper substantiation is crucial to ensure that the deduction is accepted by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) during audits.",
